      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #62217.\n\nUnder HiSparse full-ISL admission (`scheduler_reserve_full_isl`), admission reserves the request's full prompt against free host blocks at admission time, and only the imported prefix blocks are actually allocated while the async KV load is in flight:\n1. Request `first` (4 blocks, 1 imported) is admitted against 4 usable host blocks (5 total including null block) and allocates 1 host block (leaving 3 free).\n2. Request `second` (3 blocks, 1 imported) is also admitted because `3 <= 3` free host blocks, and allocates 1 host block (leaving 2 free).\n3. Once both async loads finish, `first` at the head of `kv_holding_waiting` needs 3 more host blocks (cannot fit in 2 free), while `second` needs 2 more host blocks (can fit and finish).\n\nPreviously, when `allocate_slots` returned `None` for `first` in `kv_holding_waiting`, `Scheduler.schedule()` executed `break` instead of skipping `first` and continuing to inspect the rest of `kv_holding_waiting`, permanently stalling the scheduler with `running == []`.\n\nAdditionally, `test_hisparse_admitted_async_loads_can_finish_with_nothing_running` previously used `host_num_blocks=4`, which only admitted `first` (`admitted == {\"first\"}`) and rejected `second` at admission time rather than admitting both.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Updated `test_hisparse_admitted_async_loads_can_finish_with_nothing_running` in `tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py` so both `first` and `second` are admitted (`assert admitted == {\"first\", \"second\"}`) and verified that `second` is scheduled and completes when `first` is blocked on host blocks.\n- Ran `pytest tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_remote_prefill_lifecycle.py`.\n\n### Credits & Acknowledgments\n- Full credit to **@digit50** for reporting #62217, providing the standalone CPU reproduction script, tracing the interaction between HiSparse full-ISL admission (`scheduler_reserve_full_isl`), `_inflight_prefills`, and `kv_holding_waiting` in `vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py`, and pointing out why `test_hisparse_admitted_async_loads_can_finish_with_nothing_running` (#59036) only admitted one request with `host_num_blocks=4`.\n- If @digit50 would like to open their own PR as offered in #62217, we are happy to yield/close this PR in favor of theirs or add `Co-authored-by:`.\n",
